  "notes": "Reference puzzle for weight (mw-e15.9), built with data only: the scale-plate-pair prefab, two weighted crate sets, props with weight and a signal latch that raises the portcullis. The goal is the outcome (both plates carry 20 to 100 kg together for a second), so any load works: it reads weight, never what supplies it. Equality is a window, not a comparison: the signal graph has no 'weigh against' node, so the plates share one window and the puzzle asks for both to sit in it. The 120 kg stone block overloads a plate (the window has a ceiling), the decoy that teaches the ceiling. Greybox, not story canon.",
